<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech end-July '97 budget deficit CZK 8.8bln-CTK.</title>
<headline>Czech end-July '97 budget deficit CZK 8.8bln-CTK.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech Republic's 1997 budget deficit  fell to 8.8 billion crowns at the end of July from 14.83 billion at  the end of June, the Czech news agency CTK reported the Finance Ministry  as saying on Friday.</p>
<p>Further details were not yet available. The government in April and  May agreed austerity measures with total spending cuts planned at  more than 45 billion crowns in attempt to bring the 1997 budget into  balance.</p>
<p>-- Robin Shepherd, Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
